{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q9MCI8","uniProtkbId":"EIBD_ECOLX","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2020-10-07","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2000-10-01","entryVersion":71,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Escherichia coli","taxonId":562,"lineage":["Bacteria","Pseudomonadati","Pseudomonadota","Gammaproteobacteria","Enterobacterales","Enterobacteriaceae","Escherichia"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"10722621"}],"value":"Immunoglobulin-binding protein EibD"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"21742268"}],"value":"Trimeric autotransporter adhesin EibD"},"shortNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"TAA EibD"}]},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Type 5 secretion system autotransporter EibD"}}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"10722621"}],"value":"eibD"}}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10722621"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19303642"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21742268"}],"value":"Binds (in a non-immune fashion) to the Fc portion of human IgA and IgG; binding occurs on the cell surface. Confers the ability to survive exposure to human serum exposure (PubMed:10722621). Binds to the Fc portion of human IgG, IgA and to whole mouse antibodies also via Fc (PubMed:19303642). Upon overexpression cells acquire an extra cell surface layer that forms a zipper-like contact between cells; cells autoagglutinate and form biofilm more readily, suggesting it may play a role in defense against a host (PubMed:21742268)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10722621"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"19303642"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"21742268"}],"value":"Homotrimer; can probably form mixed heterotrimers in vivo (Probable). Will form mixed heterotrimers with EibA or EibC; these are correctly located in the outer membrane and bind IgG Fc, although less well than homotrimers (PubMed:22155776). In denaturing gels runs as a band of about 210 kDa (PubMed:10722621). Binds the Fc portion of immunoglobulins; binds more than 1 Fc per subunit, can be modeled to bind 3 Fc per trimer (Probable) (PubMed:19303642)"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q9MCI8","intActId":"EBI-15935491"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q9MCI8","geneName":"eibD","intActId":"EBI-15935491"},"numberOfExperiments":3,"organismDiffer":false}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"10722621"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"19303642"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"21742268"}],"value":"The C-terminal translocator domain is localized in the outer membrane and the passenger domain is at the cell surface"}]},"subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"10722621"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"19303642"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"21742268"}],"value":"Cell surface","id":"SL-0310"}},{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"10722621"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"21742268"}],"value":"Cell outer membrane","id":"SL-0040"},"topology":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"}],"value":"Multi-pass membrane protein","id":"SL-9909"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10722621"}],"value":"In strain ECOR 9 expression is greater at 37 than 27 degrees Celsius and increases upon entry into stationary phase (at protein level). Upon expression from a plasmid in strain AB1157 (with its own leader sequence) more protein is seen at 37 than 27 degrees Celsius (at protein level)"}],"commentType":"INDUCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"P0C2W0"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"21742268"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"}],"value":"The signal peptide, cleaved at the inner membrane, guides the autotransporter protein to the periplasmic space (By similarity). Then, trimerization and insertion of the C-terminal translocator domain in the outer membrane forms a hydrophilic pore for the translocation of the passenger domain to the bacterial cell surface (PubMed:22155776). The crystallized passenger domain (residues 161-440) is an entwined, elongated trimer with a head domain, a neck and 2 extended coiled-coil regions of differing handedness separated by a saddle region. There are a number of cavities in the first (right-handed, RHcc) coiled-coil domain that may allow bending of the extended structure. Smaller cavities in the second (left-handed, LHcc) coiled-coil bind 5 Cl(-) and one water molecule. The Fc portion of IgG has been modeled to bind to the LHcc domain just under the saddle; up to 3 Fc can bind to the trimer (PubMed:21742268)"}],"commentType":"DOMAIN"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"10722621"}],"value":"Encoded in a prophage region of strain ECOR 9, upon UV treatment bacteriophage containing this gene can be isolated"}],"commentType":"MISCELLANEOUS"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the autotransporter-2 (AT-2) (TC 1.B.40) family. Eib subfamily"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"}],"features":[{"type":"Signal","location":{"start":{"value":1,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":26,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000255"}]},{"type":"Chain","location":{"start":{"value":27,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":511,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Immunoglobulin-binding protein EibD","featureId":"PRO_0000450748"},{"type":"Topological domain","location":{"start":{"value":27,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":460,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Extracellular","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":461,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":471,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Beta stranded","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":474,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":485,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Beta stranded","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":488,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":497,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Beta stranded","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"}]},{"type":"Transmembrane","location":{"start":{"value":501,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":511,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Beta stranded","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"22155776"}]},{"type":"Region","location":{"start":{"value":27,"modifier":"EXACT"},"end":{"value":417,"modifier":"EXACT"}},"description":"Surface exposed passenger domain","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"